func=jag::packethandlers::Loc::LocAddChange	func_addr=0x000edeb0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt loc-add handler; queues a LocChangeRequest with kind \e 1. Wire: [g4 middle-endian packed coord: plane\e(v&gt;&gt;0x1c)&amp;3, tileX\e(v&gt;&gt;0xe)&amp;0x3fff, tileY\ev&amp;0x3fff, 0xffffffff \e none][g4 middle-endian typeId][g1][g1 add-transformed: rotation \e v&amp;3, shape \e (v&gt;&gt;2)&amp;0x1f, high bit selects an extended float block].\nThe request is a pooled object; its shared_ptr is {control \e obj, record \e obj+0x20}, so all LocChangeRequest field offsets below are relative to obj+0x20 - which is what IsSupersededBy reads via *(shared_ptr+8). Record: +0x8 plane, +0xc tileX, +0x10 tileY, +0x14 shape, +0x15 rotation, +0x48 bool (shape bucket non-zero), +0x60 typeId, +0x64 the second wire byte, +0x68 kind (1 here), +0x70 cycle. Pending list is Client+0x198c8.
func=jag::GraphicsApp::Frame	func_addr=0x00637670	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::GraphicsApp::Frame(App* this, ? renderArg) - PROBABLE (role CERTAIN, class PROBABLE).\nPer-frame driver on the app base class shared by jag::Client and the --compileshader sibling app.\nComputes how many logic ticks are owed this frame, then runs\n  for (i \e 0; i < ticks; i++) { vt[+0xF0](this, i \e\e ticks-1);   // jag::Client::MainLogic\n                                ++*(int*)(this+0x568);\n                                ++*(int*)(this+0x528);           // clientCycle\n                                ++*(int*)(this+0x52C); }\nand afterwards vt[+0xF8](this, renderArg) followed by ++*(int*)(this+0x530) (renderCycle).\nThis is where CLIENT_CYCLE (+0x528) and CLIENT_RENDER_CYCLE (+0x530) are established: 0x528 is\nbumped once per logic tick, 0x530 once per rendered frame, and jag::Client::MainLogic forwards both\nas the (int,int) pair to the tick handler at 0x0010eaf0.\nClass name taken from the only Jagex app class present in the MSVC RTTI set\n(".?AV?$_Binder@...P8GraphicsApp@jag@@EAA_NXZPEAV34@@std@@"); not independently confirmed.
