func=jag::game::LocationRequestPendingList::ApplyLocChange	func_addr=0x00194c40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Engine const APPLY_LOC_CHANGE. Drops every pending request superseded by the incoming one, then appends it. Supersede test is outlined into IsSupersededBy: existing.kind(+0x68)\e\e4 && incoming.kind(+0x68)\e\e2 && packedKey equal, where packedKey \e ((plane(+0x8)&3 | shapeBucket) << 0xe | tileX(+0xc)) << 0xe | tileY(+0x10), plus bit 32 when (shape(+0x14) - 0x17) > 1. shapeBucket from shape: <4 or \e\e0x17 -> 0; <9 or \e\e0x18 -> 4; <0x16 -> 8; else 0xc. MSVC pre-shifts the bucket, so the Linux build's 0x40000000/0x80000000/0xc0000000 immediates do not appear here. Pending list is the vector at this+0x60/+0x68/+0x70 of 0x10-byte shared_ptr entries; growth path is FUN_000af1f0. Sibling FUN_00187e50 cancels matching requests across both the rbtree at this+0x8 and this vector without appending.
