func=jag::ClientProt::SendEventMouseClick	func_addr=0x00111ef0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Drains the head entry of the click ring buffer on MainLogicManager (client+0x198e0): ring base +0x46f0, 0x28-byte entries, head index +0x4ec4, tail +0x4ec0. Entry: +0x0 int button, +0x4 float x, +0x8 float y, +0x18 timestamp. Wire is 6 bytes: x as u16 LE (clamped 0..0xffff), y as u16 LE (clamped 0..0xffff), then (timestamp - lastSent) clamped to 0x7fff as u16 LE with the button in bit 15. lastSent is cached at this+0x20. Sibling event senders on the same object: keyboard/interface-event pump FUN_001112b0, window status FUN_00111c30.
func=jag::EventListeners::CallListeners	func_addr=0x00789510	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::EventListeners<std::function<bool(float,float)>>::CallListeners(inputHandler, x, y) -> bool.\nLocks the slot mutex at handler+0x290, walks the listener vector handler+0x278 (begin) ..\nhandler+0x280 (end), and for each non-null element invokes\n    callable \e *(void**)(*element + 0x38);\n    (*(code**)(*callable + 0x10))(callable, &x, &y);\nreturning 1 on the first listener that returns true, 0 if none consumed.\nNOTE the argument order is (&x, &y) - x first. Same std::function shape as the DoAction\ncallables: engaged pointer at +0x38, invoke at vtable slot 2 (+0x10).\nInputHandler listener-slot layout (derived, NOT the Linux 0x08 + n*0x40):\n    slot n at 0xd8 + n*0x68; within a slot: +0x00 begin, +0x08 end, +0x10 cap, +0x18 mutex.\n    slot 0  \e 0xd8  middle-button-down (walked inline by the WndProc dispatch)\n    slot 4  \e 0x278 mouse-motion (this function)\n    slot 17 \e 0x7c0 device-change (WM_DEVICECHANGE)\nEvidence: (1) identical iterate-and-stop-on-true contract to the Linux CallListeners;\n(2) the 0x68 slot stride is exact across all three observed slots ((0x278-0xd8)/0x68 \e 4,\n(0x7c0-0xd8)/0x68 \e 17) with the mutex consistently +0x18 inside the slot; (3) reached from\njag::input::Input::OnMouseMotion for every named handler and for the global handler.
func=jag::ScenePicker::TestEntityHit	func_addr=0x002fbdb0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=Settles the Entity screen-space picking block on Windows. Entity+0x14 selects the mode. Mode 0 (point): +0x30 centre X, +0x34 centre Y, +0x38 radius, circle test dx^2+dy^2 &lt;\e (radius+clickRadius)^2. Mode !\e 0 (line): +0x18/+0x1c endpoint 1, +0x20/+0x24 endpoint 2, +0x28 radius, point-to-segment distance with projection clamped to the segment. Reaches the entity as *(pickable+8) and its GraphNode via Entity+0x8. Entity vtable slots used: +0x20 (unshifted vs Linux), +0x88 IsPickable (Linux +0x90), +0x108 mark-picked (Linux +0x110) - the -8 shift applies to the later slots only, not to +0x20.
func=jag::Client::Client	func_addr=0x0001d030	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::Client::Client(Client*) - CERTAIN.\nSole constructor. Called from the app bootstrap FUN_0001b7d0 immediately after\noperator new(0x53818, 16); the result is stored into both jag::g_client (0x00e8e490) and\njag::g_app (0x00c883a8). Windows Client object size \e 0x53818 bytes.\nEvidence (3 independent):\n 1. Allocation-then-construct pair in the bootstrap, whose alternate --compileshader branch builds\n    a 0x18D20-byte sibling app from the same base - i.e. this is the game-app object.\n 2. Installs the Client vtable at +0x00 (PTR_FUN_00b4fe10) plus secondary vptrs at +0x508 and\n    +0x18D08, and stores the literal "client" (used later as the config section name in\n    Client::Init at 0x0001f9f0).\n 3. Spawns the Js5WorkerThread / MixerWorker / VorbisWorker worker threads - the client's own\n    worker set.\nFields initialised here that are load-bearing: mainState int @ +0x19F60 \e 0,\nconnection/manager pointer slots across +0x19818..+0x19A00 all zeroed (they are populated later by\nthe manager-construction pass FUN_000223c0), window size @ +0x537D8 \e 1280 x 720.\nBase sub-object occupies 0x00..0x18D20; Client-specific data starts at 0x18D08 (third vptr).
