func=jag::ProjectileList::Add	func_addr=0x0019de50	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::ProjectileList::Add - appends a projectile. this+0x8 \e jag::Client*.\nList fields: +0x10 head sentinel, +0x18 tail, +0x20/+0x28/+0x30/+0x38 node pool/freelist,\n+0x50 live count (hard cap 100 - the oldest is evicted first).\nPooled ProjectileEntity stride 0x1C0; construction is FUN_001a8d50 (the ProjectileEntity ctor,\nwhich calls jag::game::Entity::Entity). GraphNode+0x1A0 is set to the new entity (back-ptr).\nOClient.SCENE_MANAGER \e 0x19990 on Windows: client[0x19990] is the SceneManager, and\nGetActiveWorld is inlined here as `idx \e sm[0x70]; world \e sm[0x58] + idx*0x10` (shared_ptr array),\nbailing to the null-world singleton when idx \e\e -1.\nEvidence: (1) the `count \e\e 100` eviction guard and the identical intrusive-list/freelist field\nset; (2) the 0x1C0 pool element stride, identical to Linux; (3) the same 19-argument signature and\nthe same tail (push node, bump count, write the entity back-ptr into GraphNode+0x1A0).
func=jag::game::InventoryManager::GetInventory	func_addr=0x00315920	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::InventoryManager::GetInventory(this, inventoryId, secondary) -> Inventory* (NULL if absent).\nSorted vector at this+0x8 (begin) / this+0x10 (end), element stride 0x48; key at element+0x0 is\n(inventoryId * 2 | secondary). Standard lower_bound; the returned pointer is element+0x8.\nEvidence: (1) identical key packing and identical 0x48-byte-stride lower_bound to Linux\njag::game::InventoryManager::GetInventory, returning element+0x8 the same way; (2) called with\nclient[0x19988] (the InventoryManager slot) from UpdateInvPartial, which falls back to\nCreateInventory on NULL exactly as Linux does; (3) same (this, u16 id, u8 flag) argument shape.
