func=jag::input::Input::OnMouseMotion	func_addr=0x0078bb90	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::input::Input::OnMouseMotion(input, x, y). Free function, `this` \e the jag::input::Input the\nWndProc dispatch (FUN_0078a2d0) is invoked on.\njag::input::Input layout (derived here and cross-checked against the dispatch):\n    +0x08 globalHandler (InputHandler*)   +0x18 mLock (mutex)\n    +0x68 namedHandlers rbtree anchor     +0x70 rbtree begin; node value at node+0x38\n    +0xb0 mouseX          +0xb4 mouseY\n    +0xb8 consoleKey vk (dispatch compares the incoming vk against it and pre-fires 0x1ca3)\n    vtable +0x08 OnKeyDown, +0x10 OnKeyUp, +0x18 OnKeyChar  <-- RVAs STILL UNRESOLVED\nWalks the named-handler rbtree calling CallListeners(handlerValue, x, y), stops on the first\nhandler that consumes, then falls through to the global handler. Publishes the final position to\njag::input::InputState::MOUSE_X/MOUSE_Y - and only writes them when NO listener consumed the\nevent (the consumed path keeps the previously latched values).\nWARNING for the next session: the vtable at 0x00b5a690 whose slots +0x8/+0x10/+0x18 are\n0x0078c5b0 / 0x0078c940 / 0x0078c7c0 is NOT this class's vtable. 0x0078c5b0 decompiles as a\ntouch/pointer-down handler taking (this, ?, pointerId, x, y) that reaches the Input indirectly via\nthis+0x70 and dispatches through FUN_00789900 (the 3-arg listener form). Do not use those three\naddresses as the keyboard handlers.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvPartial	func_addr=0x000fbcd0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=jag::PacketHandlers::UpdateInvPartial - handler+0x0 \e jag::Client*.\nWire: g2 inventoryId, g1 flags (bit0 \e secondary inventory, bit1 \e per-slot vars follow).\nGetInventory(client[0x19988], id, flags&1), falling back to CreateInventory.\nThen, while pos < endPos: gSmart1or2 slot; count \e (g_protocolRevision < 0x3B5 ? g2 : g3);\nif count !\e 0 { objId \e g1, and if that byte \e\e 0xFF then g4; if (flags&2) varCount \e g1 }.\nPer var: g2 varId + g4 value, stored via FindOrCreateEntry into inv[0x28] + slot*0x38 + 8.\nTail: dirty-inventory ring on client[0x19958] - int[64] at +0xa8 indexed by (counter++ & 0x3f)\nat +0xb0 (the same manager UpdateStat uses, whose stat ring is at +0xc8/+0xd0).\nEvidence: (1) field-for-field identical decode ladder to Linux UpdateInvPartial, including the\n0xFF count escape and the (flags&2) var loop; (2) same GetInventory-then-CreateInventory pair and\nthe same VarDomain::FindOrCreateEntry destination arithmetic (slot*0x38 + 8); (3) same dirty-ring\ntail and the same handler sentinel return value as UpdateStat.\nOClient: INVENTORY_MANAGER \e 0x19988.
