func=jag::InterfaceManager::DrawComponentList	func_addr=0x0016faa0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	cu_index_from_entry=0	text=void DrawComponentList(longlong interfaceManagerInterior, void **componentSlotVector,\n                       int screenX, int screenY,\n                       int clipX, int clipY, int clipWidth, int clipHeight,\n                       float drawExtra)\n\nArgument mapping proven from the marshalling in the sole in-body caller DrawInterfaceSlot @0x16f990\n(call at 0x16fa7f) plus this body's own uses:\n  arg0 RCX  interior pointer - the real InterfaceManager is arg0-0x10 and Client* is at arg0-0x8.\n            The caller passes its OWN `this` verbatim (MOV RCX,RBX), and that same pointer is the\n            base for the hash fields at +0x108/+0x110. FORWARD IT UNCHANGED - do not adjust.\n  arg1 RDX  component-slot vector {begin,end}, walked at stride 0x18 (slot +0x0 removed flag,\n            +0x10 shared_ptr<Component>). Caller selects layer+0x38 when that vector is non-empty,\n            else layer+0x20 (CMOVNZ at 0x16fa47).\n  arg2 R8D  int screenX - added to component+0x50 (PARENT_REL_X) and stored at this+0x310 as the\n            drag-origin X.\n  arg3 R9D  int screenY - added to component+0x54 (PARENT_REL_Y) and stored at this+0x314.\n  arg4..7   int clipX, clipY, clipWidth, clipHeight - forwarded straight to the scissor setter\n            FUN_0046c6b0(ctx, x, y, w, h, replace), which computes x+w / y+h for the far edges.\n            ORIGIN+EXTENT, not a corner pair.\n  arg8      FLOAT, not an int. The caller marshals it MOVSS XMM0,[RSP+0xa0] -> [RSP+0x40] - a\n            stack-to-stack copy through XMM, which the compiler would never emit for an integer.\n            Forwarded as the 4th argument of the component draw virtual (vtable +0x38). Semantic\n            meaning not established.\n\nReturn: void. The sole caller does not touch RAX after the call, and DrawInterfaceSlot's other exit\npath leaves RAX undefined, so DrawInterfaceSlot is itself void and never consumes a result. This is\nweaker evidence than the explicit MOV RAX in ReadIncomingMessage/CreatePacket - noted as such.\n\nWindows arg indices for the vector / screenX / screenY match the Linux hook exactly (1 / 2 / 3);\nonly the trailing float arg8 is new on Windows.
